# 1️⃣ Merge K Sorted Lists

## 📖 Problem

You are given `k` sorted linked lists.

Merge all of them into one sorted linked list.

### Example

```text
List 1:
1 → 4 → 5

List 2:
1 → 3 → 4

List 3:
2 → 6

1 → 1 → 2 → 3 → 4 → 4 → 5 → 6

Min Heap

example

class Solution
{
public:

    struct Compare
    {
        bool operator()(ListNode* a, ListNode* b)
        {
            return a->val > b->val;
        }
    };

    ListNode* mergeKLists(
        vector<ListNode*>& lists)
    {
        priority_queue<
            ListNode*,
            vector<ListNode*>,
            Compare
        > pq;

        for(ListNode* node : lists)
        {
            if(node != NULL)
                pq.push(node);
        }

        ListNode dummy(0);
        ListNode* tail = &dummy;

        while(!pq.empty())
        {
            ListNode* current = pq.top();
            pq.pop();

            tail->next = current;
            tail = current;

            if(current->next != NULL)
            {
                pq.push(current->next);
            }
        }

        return dummy.next;
    }
};
